"""cascade generator: the published champion corpus, with a padded component riding as a second channel.

Every record is the champion's own series, drawn in order with the round's generation seed and the
trainer's own request size n, so channel 0 replays the king leg's corpus exactly: nothing is displaced
and the paired comparison against the king keeps its shared series. On a fraction q_attach of records a
component series, left-padded with its first value to the full context (the format ~93% of scored
windows reach the model in), is stacked as a second channel, making a (2, L) record.

Why a second channel: the budget is denominated in series-points, so a (C, L) record bills L -- the
component adds tokens without costing the king's corpus any budget. It also gives the variate-attention
layer gradient; with univariate data only, its Q/K never train and multivariate eval windows are
forecast with uniform cross-channel mixing, which costs this lineage on the live pool's joint windows.

The per-record attach coin uses a lazily seeded SeedSequence([seed, tag], spawn_key=(i,)) so memory
stays constant at the trainer's token_budget // min_length request size.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import json
import sys as _sys
import types as _types
from collections.abc import Iterator
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np

